AskUserQuestion, header `rdp-lang`:

**"Merge and deploy to ccs-it in 15 minutes" would set aside three rules: a report that skipped required skills is redone (manifest §5); review by the other model family before any merge request (CLAUDE.md); my own check run and the canary sequence (§8). What do I do?**

1. **Keep the gates; you test after the weekend (Recommended).** Redo about 40 min, review about 20 min, my own check run, then the merge decision and canary by the normal procedure. Nothing is merged tonight on this report.
2. **Keep the gates; you test tonight.** Same steps; ccs-it is ready at about 02:30 at the earliest, and I ping you with the test steps.
3. **One-off waiver: merge 4ba90e0 as is.** No redo and no review. I run the offline checks, merge, and deploy from main (dry run, real run, verification, re-run). Ready in about 35 min, not 15. If the code is wrong, RDP login on the desktops it lands on may break; rollback is reverting the merge and redeploying.

